data.content:
Done. Here's the summary:

**`SortableList.razor`** — renders a `<ul>` with each item showing `ItemTemplate` content plus "Move Up" / "Move Down" buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — generic `TItem` code-behind that:
- Accepts `Items` (read-only) and copies it internally in `OnParametersSet`
- Never mutates the original list
- Swaps items on button click and fires `OnOrderChanged` with the new list as `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`

Usage matches your example:
```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
